<button type="button" aria-label="Increase">+</button>
</span>
</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="recap">🏠 <b>House</b> · 120 m² living area · <b>2 floors</b> · footprint ~60 m² · ceiling 2.5 m → exterior walls ≈ <b>194 m²</b> · roof ≈ <b>84 m²</b>
<span style="color:var(--faint)"> (incl. ~60 m² upstairs)</span>
<div style="margin-top:6px">→ <b>7 rooms</b> in total · <b>2 bathrooms</b> (incl. 1 in a suite) · 10 exterior doors &amp; windows</div>
<div style="margin-top:6px">📍 <b>Paris &amp; inner ring</b> · labor +20%</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="intro">Open the trades you need, check the work items, adjust the quantities. Prices shown <b>excl. VAT</b>. On every item you can do yourself, electrical, load-bearing walls and roof framing included, choose <b>“Hire out”</b> (contractor) or <b>“DIY”</b> — both prices are shown. Done yourself, a masonry, roof framing, roofing or exterior door and window item is not covered by the 10-year structural warranty; for a load-bearing wall or roof framing, an engineering study is recommended.</div>
